  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "In a small business, the seven employees earn the following wages per week:\n\n$\\$300$, $\\$490$, $\\$520$, $\\$590$, $\\$660$, $\\$680$, $\\$970$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p43-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Is the wage of $\\$970$ an outlier for this set of data? Justify your answer with calculations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Yes. $\\$970$ exceeds the upper fence of $\\$965$.",
          "worked": "The wages are ordered: $300,490,520,590,660,680,970$. Excluding the median, $590$, the lower and upper halves give $Q_1=490$ and $Q_3=680$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{IQR}&=Q_3-Q_1\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}&=680-490\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}&=190\\end{align*}$$\n\nTo check for upper outliers:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Upper fence}&=Q_3+1.5\\times\\mathrm{IQR}\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=680+1.5(190)\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=680+285\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=965\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $970>965$, the wage of $\\$970$ is an outlier.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Each employee receives a $\\$20$ pay increase.\n\nWhat effect will this have on the standard deviation?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No effect. The spread does not change.",
          "worked": "The standard deviation is unchanged. Adding $\\$20$ to every wage also increases the mean by $\\$20$, so each wage's deviation from the mean stays the same.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      }
    ]
  },
